What follows is a repost of information concerning magic markers.
The info comes from the source code.
 
Stefan Larsson's problem is addressed in the first paragraph.
Information on blessed/cursed status are dealt with, too, and
show where John David Galt missed the mark.

SPOILER ALERT

 
WARNING:  Say you just made a blank scroll by #dipping it.  Check that
your inventory lists it as "blank paper" and not the "unknown" name
corresponding to blank paper.  If it doesn't say "blank paper", read
it first!  If you don't, and attempt to write on it, you'll get:   
  "In your haste, you rip the scroll to pieces."
and lose the blank scroll. 
 
The actual "cost" for using a magic marker to write a particular
scroll varies randomly between the min. and max. values (inclusively)
given in the table below. 
 
 
Scroll type		Min cost	Max cost
 
MAIL			  1
LIGHT			  4		  7
DETECTION		  4		  7
FOOD DETECTION		  4		  7
MAGIC MAPPING		  4		  7
AMNESIA			  4		  7
FIRE			  4		  7
DESTROY ARMOR		  5		  9
CREATE MONSTER		  5		  9
PUNISHMENT		  5		  9
CONFUSE MONSTER		  6		 11
IDENTIFY		  7		 13
ENCHANT ARMOR		  8		 15
REMOVE CURSE		  8		 15
ENCHANT WEAPON		  8		 15
CHARGING		  8		 15
SCARE MONSTER		 10		 19
TAMING			 10		 19
TELEPORTATION		 10		 19
GENOCIDE		 15		 29
 
 
If the marker does not have at least the min. value, you'll get:
  "Your marker is too dry to write that!"
You will not have used any ink, and you'll still have the blank
scroll.
 
If it has more than the min., but not enough for the (randomly 
determined) actual, you'll get:
  "Your marker dries out!"
  "The scroll is useless and disappears!"
The marker will now be at zero, and the scroll will be gone.
 
There is a chance that you can write a scroll you haven't seen yet.
For wizards, it's 1 in 3 (33%); for others, it's 1 in 15.  If it 
doesn't work, you'll get:
  "You don't know how to write that!"
  "You write '--- was here' and the scroll disappears."
You will have used up ink as if you had actually written the scroll,
and the scroll will be gone.
 
The "cursed" status of the final scroll can be determined from the 
following table:
 
              Pen
            B  U  C
          __________
        B | B  B  U
Scroll  U | B  U  C
        C | U  C  C
 


